IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `sis-ins-dates`

-- Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Act 1993 (Cth) and Superannuation Industry (Supervision) Regulations 1994:
-- insurance inside super, total and permanent disablement (TPD) and income protection claims.
-- Baseline encoding, from the seat of the fund member who is, or may be, claiming on insurance held through super.
-- A second encoding beside ../baseline-2026-10/ (conditions of release, death benefits, the ss 68AAA-68AAD opt-in
-- rules), which is untouched. See NOTES.md for scope, the fork register and the findings.
--
-- Answers are MAYBE BOOLEAN where the rulings of 2026-11-04 and 2026-11-05 apply: JUST FALSE where the text itself
-- says no, NOTHING where it is silent or the case falls outside its scope.

§ `Insurance inside super: what the member can expect and claim`

§§ `s 52(1), (7) -- the insurance covenants in my fund's governing rules`

-- s 52(1): the governing rules of a "registrable superannuation entity" are taken to contain the covenants in s 52.
-- A registrable superannuation entity is, in plain terms, an APRA-regulated fund; a self managed fund is not one.
-- s 52(7)(d): each trustee covenants "to do everything that is reasonable to pursue an insurance claim for the benefit
-- of a beneficiary, if the claim has a reasonable prospect of success". Whether it has such a prospect is not decided
-- here: it is asked.
@export Must my fund do everything reasonable to pursue my insurance claim, such as a TPD, income protection or death claim (SIS Act s 52(1), (7)(d))?
GIVEN `my fund is a registrable superannuation entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your fund an APRA-regulated fund (not a self managed super fund)?
      `my claim has a reasonable prospect of success` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does your insurance claim have a reasonable prospect of success?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my fund pursue my insurance claim` IS
    IF (NOT `my fund is a registrable superannuation entity`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `my claim has a reasonable prospect of success`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 52(7)(c): each trustee covenants "to only offer or acquire insurance of a particular kind, or at a particular level,
-- if the cost of the insurance does not inappropriately erode the retirement income of beneficiaries". Whether the
-- cost erodes it inappropriately is a judgment, asked as a fact.
@export Does the cost covenant stop my fund offering or acquiring this insurance for me (SIS Act s 52(7)(c))?
GIVEN `my fund is a registrable superannuation entity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is your fund an APRA-regulated fund (not a self managed super fund)?
      `the cost inappropriately erodes retirement income` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Does the cost of this insurance, of this kind or at this level, inappropriately erode members' retirement income?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the cost covenant stop my fund offering this insurance` IS
    IF (NOT `my fund is a registrable superannuation entity`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE JUST `the cost inappropriately erodes retirement income`

§§ `reg 4.07C, 4.07D -- the kinds of insurance my fund may provide`

-- reg 4.07C: an "insured benefit" is "a right for the member's benefits to be increased on the realisation of a risk".
-- reg 4.07D(2): a trustee of a regulated superannuation fund "must not provide an insured benefit ... unless the insured
-- event is consistent with a condition of release specified in item 102 [death], 102A [terminal medical condition], 103
-- [permanent incapacity] or 109 [temporary incapacity] of Schedule 1".
DECLARE `An insured event` IS ONE OF
    `my death`                                   -- item 102
    `a terminal medical condition`               -- item 102A
    `permanent incapacity`                       -- item 103: unlikely ever again to work in a job I am reasonably qualified for (reg 1.03C)
    `temporary incapacity`                       -- item 109: ill-health that stopped my work, short of permanent incapacity
    `another event`                              -- e.g. trauma cover, or a disablement wider than permanent incapacity

GIVEN `the event` IS AN `An insured event`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the event is consistent with a condition of release in items 102, 102A, 103 or 109` IS
    CONSIDER `the event`
    WHEN `another event` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- reg 4.07D(3): (2) "does not apply to (a) the continued provision of benefits to members who joined a fund before 1 July
-- 2014; or (b) the provision of benefits under an approval granted before 1 July 2014 under subparagraph 62(1)(b)(v)".
@export Does the Regulations' list of permitted insured events stop my fund insuring me against this event (SIS Regulations reg 4.07D)?
GIVEN `the event` IS AN `An insured event` @desc The event the cover pays on: my death, a terminal medical condition, permanent incapacity, temporary incapacity (income protection), or another event (e.g. trauma cover)
      `the day I joined the fund` IS A DATE @desc The day you joined the fund (ISO date)
      `the cover is under an approval granted before 1 July 2014` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the cover provided under a Regulator's approval under s 62(1)(b)(v) granted before 1 July 2014?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does reg 4.07D stop my fund insuring me against this event` IS
    IF     `is before` `the day I joined the fund` (`the date` 1 7 2014)
        OR `the cover is under an approval granted before 1 July 2014`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE JUST (NOT (`the event is consistent with a condition of release in items 102, 102A, 103 or 109` `the event`))

§§ `reg 4.07E -- self-insurance: must my cover be backed by an insurance policy`

-- reg 4.07E(2): a fund that on 1 July 2013 did not self-insure a risk may, on and after 1 July 2013, provide an insured
-- benefit for it "only if the provision of the benefit is fully supported by an insurance policy provided by an
-- insurer". (3): (2) does not apply, on or before 1 July 2016, to a member transferred from a fund that self-insured the
-- member into a successor (or Part 33) fund that did not.
-- (4): a fund that on 1 July 2013 self-insured the risk is held to the same rule "on and after 1 July 2016". (7): not if
-- a government provides or guarantees the insured benefit. (8): not for defined benefit members if APRA had not, on or
-- before 1 July 2013, prohibited self-insurance for them by a licence condition and the fund self-insured them on 1 July
-- 2013.
DECLARE `My fund's cover` HAS
    `the fund self-insured this risk on 1 July 2013`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `I was transferred in from a fund that self-insured me`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `a government provides or guarantees the insured benefit`     IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a defined benefit member`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `APRA had prohibited self-insurance for defined benefit members by 1 July 2013` IS A BOOLEAN

@export On this day, may my fund provide my insured benefit only if an insurance policy fully supports it (SIS Regulations reg 4.07E)?
GIVEN `the cover` IS A `My fund's cover` @desc Whether your fund self-insured the risk on 1 July 2013, how you came into the fund, any government guarantee, and defined benefit membership
      `the day` IS A DATE @desc The day asked about (ISO date)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my cover be backed by an insurance policy` IS
    IF (NOT (`the cover`'s `the fund self-insured this risk on 1 July 2013`))
    THEN IF `is before` `the day` (`the date` 1 7 2013)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF     `the cover`'s `I was transferred in from a fund that self-insured me`
                 AND `is on or before` `the day` (`the date` 1 7 2016)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF `is before` `the day` (`the date` 1 7 2016)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the cover`'s `a government provides or guarantees the insured benefit`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF     `the cover`'s `I am a defined benefit member`
                      AND (NOT (`the cover`'s `APRA had prohibited self-insurance for defined benefit members by 1 July 2013`))
                   THEN JUST FALSE
                   ELSE JUST TRUE

-- reg 4.07E(9): "Despite subregulation (4)", a beneficiary in column 2 immediately before 1 July 2016 keeps the
-- entitlement in column 3: item 1 receiving an insured benefit -- continue to receive it; item 2 having lodged a claim --
-- have it determined and receive the benefit if the trustee so determines; item 3 eligible to claim -- lodge a claim,
-- have it determined and receive the benefit if the trustee so determines.
DECLARE `My position immediately before 1 July 2016` IS ONE OF
    `I was receiving an insured benefit`
    `I had lodged a claim for an insured benefit`
    `I was eligible to make a claim for an insured benefit`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `My entitlement under reg 4.07E(9)` IS ONE OF
    `to continue to receive the insured benefit`
    `to have the claim determined, and to receive the benefit if the trustee so determines`
    `to lodge a claim, have it determined, and receive the benefit if the trustee so determines`
    `no entitlement under reg 4.07E(9)`

@export My fund self-insured my cover: what does the transition rule keep for me from 1 July 2016 (SIS Regulations reg 4.07E(9))?
GIVEN `the fund self-insured this risk on 1 July 2013` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your fund self-insure this risk (carry it itself, without an insurer) on 1 July 2013?
      `my position` IS A `My position immediately before 1 July 2016` @desc Immediately before 1 July 2016, were you receiving an insured benefit, had you lodged a claim, or were you eligible to claim?
GIVETH A MAYBE `My entitlement under reg 4.07E(9)`
DECIDE `What does reg 4.07E(9) keep for me` IS
    IF (NOT `the fund self-insured this risk on 1 July 2013`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `my position`
         WHEN `I was receiving an insured benefit` THEN JUST `to continue to receive the insured benefit`
         WHEN `I had lodged a claim for an insured benefit` THEN JUST `to have the claim determined, and to receive the benefit if the trustee so determines`
         WHEN `I was eligible to make a claim for an insured benefit` THEN JUST `to lodge a claim, have it determined, and receive the benefit if the trustee so determines`
         WHEN `none of these` THEN JUST `no entitlement under reg 4.07E(9)`

§§ `s 68AA(2)-(4) -- conditions on my MySuper death and TPD cover`

-- s 68AA(1) requires a MySuper member's permanent incapacity benefit and death benefit, provided by insurance. (2): the
-- trustees "are not required to provide" either "if the conditions determined under subsection (3) in relation to the
-- benefit are not met". (3): they "may determine reasonable conditions". (4): conditions "are reasonable if they are the
-- same as the terms and conditions of the policy of insurance taken out to provide the benefit". (9): the section does
-- not apply to a defined benefit member, or to an ADF Super member of the Permanent Forces or a continuous full-time
-- Reservist.
DECLARE `My MySuper claim` HAS
    `I am a MySuper member`                                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `I am a defined benefit member or an excluded ADF Super member`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee determined conditions for the benefit`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conditions are the same as the insurance policy's terms`    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the conditions are otherwise reasonable`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `I meet the conditions`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My MySuper claim`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conditions are reasonable conditions under s 68AA(3)` IF
        `the claim`'s `the trustee determined conditions for the benefit`
    AND (   `the claim`'s `the conditions are the same as the insurance policy's terms`
         OR `the claim`'s `the conditions are otherwise reasonable`)

@export Is my fund excused from providing my MySuper death or TPD benefit because I do not meet its conditions (SIS Act s 68AA(2)-(4), (9))?
GIVEN `the claim` IS A `My MySuper claim` @desc Your MySuper membership, the conditions the trustee set for the benefit, and whether you meet them
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is my fund excused from my MySuper death or TPD benefit` IS
    IF     (NOT (`the claim`'s `I am a MySuper member`))
        OR `the claim`'s `I am a defined benefit member or an excluded ADF Super member`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `the conditions are reasonable conditions under s 68AA(3)` `the claim`
         THEN JUST (NOT (`the claim`'s `I meet the conditions`))
         ELSE JUST FALSE

§§ `reg 6.01(2), Schedule 1 item 109 -- income protection: temporary incapacity`

-- reg 6.01(2): "temporary incapacity, in relation to a member who has ceased to be gainfully employed (including a member
-- who has ceased temporarily to receive any gain or reward under a continuing arrangement for the member to be gainfully
-- employed), means ill-health (whether physical or mental) that caused the member to cease to be gainfully employed but
-- does not constitute permanent incapacity".
-- Permanent incapacity (reg 1.03C) turns on the trustee being reasonably satisfied that the member's ill-health makes it
-- unlikely the member will ever again be gainfully employed in work they are reasonably qualified for; asked as a fact.
DECLARE `My incapacity` HAS
    `I have stopped work, or stopped being paid under a continuing arrangement` IS A BOOLEAN
    `ill-health caused me to stop`                                              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the trustee is satisfied my incapacity is permanent`                       IS A BOOLEAN

@export Am I temporarily incapacitated, as the SIS Regulations define it for income protection (reg 6.01(2))?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My incapacity` @desc Whether you have stopped work or pay, whether ill-health caused it, and whether the trustee accepts it is permanent
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I temporarily incapacitated` IS
    JUST (    `me`'s `I have stopped work, or stopped being paid under a continuing arrangement`
          AND `me`'s `ill-health caused me to stop`
          AND (NOT (`me`'s `the trustee is satisfied my incapacity is permanent`)))

-- Schedule 1 item 109, cashing restriction on preserved benefits: "A non-commutable income stream cashed from the
-- regulated superannuation fund for: (a) the purpose of continuing (in whole or part) the gain or reward which the
-- member was receiving before the temporary incapacity; and (b) a period not exceeding the period of incapacity from
-- employment of the kind engaged in immediately before the temporary incapacity".
DECLARE `A form of payment` IS ONE OF
    `a non-commutable income stream`
    `a commutable income stream`
    `a lump sum`

DECLARE `My income protection payment` HAS
    `the form`                                       IS A `A form of payment`
    `the monthly amount`                             IS A NUMBER
    `my monthly pay before the incapacity`           IS A NUMBER
    `the last day paid for`                          IS A DATE
    `my incapacity has ended`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `the last day of my incapacity`                  IS A DATE

@export May my fund pay me this temporary incapacity (income protection) benefit from my preserved super, in this form, amount and period (SIS Regulations Schedule 1 item 109)?
GIVEN `me` IS A `My incapacity` @desc Whether you have stopped work or pay, whether ill-health caused it, and whether the trustee accepts it is permanent
      `the payment` IS A `My income protection payment` @desc The form, monthly amount and last day of the benefit; your monthly pay before; whether and when your incapacity for your usual work ended
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my fund pay my temporary incapacity benefit this way` IS
    IF `Am I temporarily incapacitated` `me` EQUALS JUST FALSE
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF (NOT (`the payment`'s `the form` EQUALS `a non-commutable income stream`))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF     `the payment`'s `my incapacity has ended`
                 AND `is before` (`the payment`'s `the last day of my incapacity`) (`the payment`'s `the last day paid for`)
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF `the payment`'s `the monthly amount` GREATER THAN `the payment`'s `my monthly pay before the incapacity`
                   THEN NOTHING
                   ELSE JUST TRUE

§§ `ss 29V(1), (9), 29VA(10), 29VC(1) -- insurance fees in my MySuper product`

-- s 29V(9): "A fee is an insurance fee if: (a) the fee relates directly to either or both of ... (i) insurance premiums
-- paid by the trustee ... in relation to a member or members ... (ii) costs incurred by the trustee ... in relation to
-- the provision of insurance for a member or members ...; and (b) the fee does not relate to any part of a premium paid
-- or cost incurred in relation to a life policy or a contract of insurance that relates to a benefit to the member that
-- is based on the performance of an investment rather than the realisation of a risk; and (c) the premiums and costs to
-- which the fee relates are not otherwise charged as an administration fee, an investment fee, a switching fee, an
-- activity fee or an advice fee."
DECLARE `A fee` HAS
    `it relates directly to insurance premiums or insurance costs for me`   IS A BOOLEAN
    `it relates to an investment-linked policy`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `those premiums or costs are charged as another kind of fee`            IS A BOOLEAN
    `the amount`                                                            IS A NUMBER
    `the cost recovery amount`                                              IS A NUMBER

@export Is this fee an insurance fee, as the SIS Act defines it (s 29V(9))?
GIVEN `the fee` IS A `A fee` @desc What the fee relates to and how it is charged
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this fee an insurance fee` IS
    JUST (    `the fee`'s `it relates directly to insurance premiums or insurance costs for me`
          AND (NOT (`the fee`'s `it relates to an investment-linked policy`))
          AND (NOT (`the fee`'s `those premiums or costs are charged as another kind of fee`)))

-- s 29VA(1): a fee may be charged in relation to a MySuper product "only ... if it satisfies one of the charging rules";
-- (10): the insurance fee rule is satisfied if the fee is an insurance fee relating directly to premiums or costs for "a
-- member", the member holds a MySuper product, and the fee is charged to the member. s 29VC(1): an insurance fee charged
-- to a member in relation to a MySuper product "must be no more than it would be if it were charged on a cost recovery
-- basis". The cost recovery amount is asked (the regulations under s 29VC(2) on working it out are not encoded).
@export May my fund charge me this insurance fee in my MySuper product (SIS Act ss 29V, 29VA(10), 29VC(1))?
GIVEN `I hold a MySuper product` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the fee charged in relation to your MySuper product?
      `the fee` IS A `A fee` @desc What the fee relates to, its amount and what it would be on a cost recovery basis (dollars)
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `May my fund charge me this insurance fee in MySuper` IS
    IF (NOT `I hold a MySuper product`)
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF `Is this fee an insurance fee` `the fee` EQUALS JUST FALSE
         THEN NOTHING
         ELSE JUST (`the fee`'s `the amount` AT MOST `the fee`'s `the cost recovery amount`)

§§ `s 55(3)-(7) -- suing for loss from a breach of covenant (e.g. a claim not pursued)`

-- s 55(3): "a person who suffers loss or damage as a result of conduct of another person that was engaged in in
-- contravention of subsection 54B(1), 54B(2) or 54C(1) may recover the amount of the loss or damage by action against
-- that other person or against any person involved in the contravention". (4): unless (4A)-(4D) apply, the action "may
-- be begun at any time within 6 years after the day on which the cause of action arose".
-- (4A): an action against a director of a corporate trustee for contravening a director's covenant (s 52A(2), or one
-- prescribed under s 54A about directors) "may be brought only with the leave of the court"; (4B): leave may be sought
-- "within 6 years after the day on which the cause of action arose"; (4D): the court may fix the period for the action.

-- The last day of the 6 years after the day the cause of action arose: the period starts the next day and ends on the
-- same date six years on (a 29 February cause gives 28 February).
@export What is the last day I can begin my action, or seek the court's leave, to recover loss from a breach of covenant (SIS Act s 55(4), (4B))?
GIVEN `the day the cause of action arose` IS A DATE @desc The day your cause of action arose, e.g. the day you suffered the loss (ISO date)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `The last day to begin my s 55 action` IS
    `the day N months after` `the day the cause of action arose` 72

DECLARE `My s 55 action` HAS
    `I suffered loss as a result of conduct in breach of a covenant`        IS A BOOLEAN
    `I sue a director of a corporate trustee for breach of a director's covenant` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the court has given leave`                                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the cause of action arose`                                     IS A DATE
    `the day I begin, or seek leave`                                        IS A DATE

@export Can I bring an action under the SIS Act to recover my loss from a breach of covenant, such as a claim my fund did not pursue (SIS Act s 55(3)-(4B))?
GIVEN `the action` IS A `My s 55 action` @desc Whether the loss came from a breach of covenant, whom you sue, any leave, and the dates
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Can I bring my s 55 action` IS
    IF (NOT (`the action`'s `I suffered loss as a result of conduct in breach of a covenant`))
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE IF (NOT (`is on or before` (`the action`'s `the day I begin, or seek leave`) (`The last day to begin my s 55 action` (`the action`'s `the day the cause of action arose`))))
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF     `the action`'s `I sue a director of a corporate trustee for breach of a director's covenant`
                 AND (NOT (`the action`'s `the court has given leave`))
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 55(5), (6): "It is a defence to an action for loss or damage suffered by a person as a result of the making of an
-- investment" (5), or "of the management of any reserves" (6), "if the defendant establishes that the defendant has
-- complied with all of the covenants ... that apply to the defendant in relation to each act, or failure to act, that
-- resulted in the loss or damage". (7): whether the action is under (3) "or otherwise".
DECLARE `The source of my loss` IS ONE OF
    `the making of an investment`
    `the management of reserves`
    `something else, e.g. how an insurance claim was handled`

@export Does the trustee have the SIS Act's compliance defence to my action for loss (SIS Act s 55(5)-(7))?
GIVEN `the source` IS A `The source of my loss` @desc What caused your loss: an investment, the management of reserves, or something else (such as how your insurance claim was handled)
      `the defendant shows it complied with every covenant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Has the trustee established that it complied with all the covenants that applied to each act or omission that caused the loss?
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does the trustee have the s 55 compliance defence` IS
    CONSIDER `the source`
    WHEN `something else, e.g. how an insurance claim was handled` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST `the defendant shows it complied with every covenant`

§§ `s 101 -- complaints about my claim`

-- s 101(1): "Each trustee of a regulated superannuation fund other than a self managed superannuation fund or of an
-- exempt public sector superannuation scheme that has elected to join the AFCA scheme, or of an approved deposit fund:
-- (a) must be a member of the AFCA scheme; and (b) must have an internal dispute resolution procedure that complies with
-- [the Corporations Act standards]; and (c) [give ASIC information] ...; and (d) must ensure that written reasons are
-- given, in accordance with requirements specified under subsection (1B) ..., for any decision of the trustee (or failure
-- by the trustee to make a decision) relating to a complaint." (1A): "(a) to (c) do not apply to a trustee if the trustee
-- is required under the Corporations Act 2001 to have a dispute resolution system complying with subsection 912A(2) or
-- 1017G(2)". Who gets the reasons and by when are in ASIC's instrument under (1B), not deposited.
DECLARE `My fund's kind` IS ONE OF
    `an APRA-regulated superannuation fund`
    `a self managed superannuation fund`
    `an exempt public sector scheme that has elected to join AFCA`
    `an exempt public sector scheme that has not elected to join AFCA`
    `an approved deposit fund`

GIVEN `the kind` IS A `My fund's kind`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 101(1) applies to my fund's trustee` IS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `a self managed superannuation fund` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an exempt public sector scheme that has not elected to join AFCA` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

@export Must my fund ensure written reasons are given for its decision on my complaint, or for its failure to decide it (SIS Act s 101(1)(d))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `My fund's kind` @desc What kind of fund it is
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must my fund give written reasons on my complaint` IS
    `s 101(1) applies to my fund's trustee` `the kind`

DECLARE `Where my fund's AFCA and complaints duties come from` IS ONE OF
    `this Act, s 101(1)(a)-(c)`
    `the Corporations Act, not s 101 (s 101(1A))`
    `s 101 does not impose them`

@export Must my fund belong to AFCA and have an internal complaints procedure under this Act, or does the Corporations Act govern that (SIS Act s 101(1)(a)-(c), (1A))?
GIVEN `the kind` IS A `My fund's kind` @desc What kind of fund it is
      `the trustee must have a Corporations Act dispute resolution system` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is the trustee required under the Corporations Act 2001 to have a dispute resolution system complying with s 912A(2) or s 1017G(2)?
GIVETH A MAYBE `Where my fund's AFCA and complaints duties come from`
DECIDE `Where do my fund's AFCA duties come from` IS
    CONSIDER `s 101(1) applies to my fund's trustee` `the kind`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
        IF `the trustee must have a Corporations Act dispute resolution system`
        THEN JUST `the Corporations Act, not s 101 (s 101(1A))`
        ELSE JUST `this Act, s 101(1)(a)-(c)`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST `s 101 does not impose them`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
